  "summary": "The intended positive-defect hypothesis is missing from the literal E1 problem, but the response itself explicitly identifies that omission and does not claim the intended target is solved.",
  "review_status": "interpretation_check_pending",
  "review_note": "Selected response explicitly disclaims closure of the intended gate. Recover the earlier malformed E1 proposal if the record is to represent a source-generation error.",
  "original": {
    "excerpt": "# Verdict: **PROVED — for \\((E1)\\) exactly as stated**\n\nThe literal existential statement \\((E1)\\) is true. The decisive issue is that \\((E1)\\) imposes no upper bound on \\(\\eta\\), hence no small-\\(A\\) or positive-gap condition. One may choose \\(A=m\\), at which point the one-copy bound and the orbit-block ratio bound become universally true.\n\nThis does **not** settle the physically relevant gate from Round 1. The strengthened statement with\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\log_2m}{m}>2\\log_2 A\n\\qquad\\Longleftrightarrow\\qquad\nA^2<m^{1/m}\n\\tag{Gap}\n$$\n\n[...]\n\n## 7. Why this does not close the intended finite gate\n\nThe construction above has\n\n$$\nA=m,\n$$\n\nso\n\n$$\n2\\log_2A=2\\log_2m\n$$\n\nwhile\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\log_2m}{m}\\ll2\\log_2m.\n$$\n\nIt is maximally outside the positive-gap regime.\n\nThe intended strengthened statement should include\n\n$$",
    "context": "The intended channel-purity gate requires the positive-defect condition A^2<m^(1/m). The displayed response explicitly distinguishes its literal E1 statement from that intended gate.",
    "locator": "round-02-response.md, lines 1–12, 1154–1178"
  },
  "witness": {
    "explanation": "The intended positive-defect hypothesis is missing from the literal E1 problem, but the response itself explicitly identifies that omission and does not claim the intended target is solved.",
    "evidence": "For m>1, A=m yields A^2=m^2>m^(1/m), so the literal E1 witness cannot establish a positive defect. However, the original response says exactly this and explicitly states that the intended strengthened gate remains unresolved. The source-bound issue is the malformed problem statement; the selected response is not evidence of a false solution claim.",
    "scope": "argument_invalid"
  },
